The genealogy of Jesus Christ.
This is a genealogical record of the lineage of Jesus Christ's family. He is the son of David. He is also the son of Abraham.
Abraham is the father of Isaac. Isaac is the father of Jacob. Jacob is the father of Judah and his brothers.
Judah fathered Perez and Zerah. Their mother was Tamar. Perez fathered Hezron. Hezron fathered Ram.
Ram was the father of Amminadab; Amminadab was the father of Nahshon; Nahshon was the father of Salmon.
Salmon was the father of Boaz. Rahab was the mother of Boaz. Boaz was the father of Obed. Ruth was the mother of Obed. Obed was the father of Jesse.
And Jesse was the father of King David. David was the father of Solomon. The mother of Solomon was the wife of Uriah.
Solomon is the father of Rehoboam. Rehoboam is the father of Abijah. Abijah is the father of Asa.
Asa was the father of Jehoshaphat. Jehoshaphat was the father of Joram. Joram was the father of Uzziah.
Azariah is the father of Jotham. Jotham is the father of Ahaz. Ahaz is the father of Hezekiah.
Hezekiah is the father of Manasseh. Manasseh is the father of Amon. Amon is the father of Josiah.
Josiah was the father of Jehoiakim and his brothers. At that time, the Jewish people were forced to go to Babylon.
Afterward, the family line continued. Jehoiakim was the father of Shealtiel. Shealtiel was the father of Zerubbabel.
Zerubbabel is the father of Abiud. Abiud is the father of Eliakim. Eliakim is the father of Azor.
Azor is the father of Zadok. Zadok is the father of Akim. Akim is the father of Eliud.
Eliud is the father of Eliezer. Eliezer is the father of Matan. Matan is the father of Jacob.
Jacob was the father of Joseph. Joseph was the husband of Mary. And Mary gave birth to Jesus who is called the Christ.
There were 14 generations from Abraham to David. There were 14 from David until the Jewish people had to go to Babylon. There were 14 from that time to Christ. Jesus Christ was born.
Thus the birth of Jesus Christ came about. His mother was Mary, and Joseph had promised to marry her. But before they began to live together, it became clear that she would become pregnant. She became pregnant through the power of the Holy Spirit.
Her husband Joseph was a good man. He did not want to bring her shame in public. So he planned to quietly divorce her.
Joseph was not contemplating this, when an angel of the Lord appeared to him in a dream. The angel said, "Joseph, son of David, do not be afraid to take Mary into your home as your wife. The child within her is from the Holy Spirit."
She is pregnant with a son. You must name him Jesus. This is because he will save his people from their sins."
All this was to fulfil what the Lord had said, that it would happen. He said this through the prophet.
