When they saw the star, they were filled with joy.
The wise men went to the house. There they saw the child with his mother Mary. They bowed down and worshipped him. Then they opened their treasures. They gave him gold, frankincense, myrrh.
But God warned them in a dream not to return to Herod. So they returned to their country by another route. Jesus's family fled to Egypt.
After the wise men left, Joseph saw a dream. In the dream, an angel of the Lord appeared to him. "Get up!" the angel said. "Take the child and his mother and flee to Egypt. Stay there until I tell you to return. Herod is searching for the child. He wants to kill him."
Joseph got up. During the night, he left for Egypt with the child and his mother Mary.
They remained there until the death of King Herod. Then the word of the Lord, which He spoke through the prophet, came to pass: "I have led My son out of Egypt." (Hosea 11:1)
Herod understood that the wise men had deceived him. His anger became intense. He gave orders concerning Bethlehem and the surrounding region. All the male children who were two years old and under were to be killed. This was in agreement with the time that the wise men had seen the star.
