Jesus replied, "Let it be so now. It is proper for us to do this. He is fulfilling God's holy plan." Then John agreed.
As soon as Jesus was baptized, he went up out of the water. At that moment, the heavens were opened. Jesus saw the Spirit of God descending on him like a dove.
A voice from heaven said, "This is my son, whom I love; with him I am well pleased."
Jesus is being tested.
The Holy Spirit led Jesus into the wilderness. There the devil tempted him.
After 40 days and 40 nights of not eating, Jesus was hungry.
The tempter came to him and said, "If you are the Son of God, command these stones to become loaves of bread."
Jesus answered, "It is written, 'Man shall not live by bread alone. But by every word that proceeds from the mouth of God.'" (Deuteronomy 8:3)
Then the devil took Jesus to the holy city. He made him stand on the highest point of the temple.
He said: "If you are the Son of God, throw yourself down from here. For it is written: 'He will command his angels concerning you, to guard you carefully; they will carry you in their hands, so that you will not strike your foot against a stone.' " (Psalm 91:11, 12)
Jesus answered, "It is also written, 'You shall not tempt the Lord your God.' " (Deuteronomy 6:16)
Finally, the devil took Jesus to a very high mountain. He showed him all the kingdoms of the world and their glory.
He said, "If you worship me and serve me, I will give you all of this."
Jesus said to him, "Get behind me, Satan! For it is written: 'Worship the Lord your God, and serve him only.' " (Deuteronomy 6:13)
Then the devil departed from Jesus. And behold, the angels came and ministered to him. Jesus begins to preach.
