Jesus is Lord of the Sabbath.
One Saturday, Jesus walked through the grain fields. His disciples were hungry. So they began to break off some heads of grain and eat them.
The Pharisees saw this. They said to Jesus, "Look! It is against the law to do this on the Sabbath. But your disciples are doing it anyway!"
Jesse answered, "You weren't there when David did it? He and his men were hungry."
He entered the house of God. He and his men ate the holy bread. Only the priests were allowed to eat it.
Haven't you read the law? It tells us how the priests in the temple should do their work every Sabbath day. But they are not considered guilty.
I tell you that someone who is more important than the temple is here.
The Bible says, "I desire mercy and not sacrifice." (Hosea 6:6) You do not know what these words mean. If you did know, you would not bring charges against people who are not guilty.
"The Son of man is Lord of the Sabbath."
From that place, Jesus went to their synagogue.
